; Two zones delegated, neither with a DS, so everything below is
; insecure.  That is on purpose: the question here is how a resolver
; reads a response, and signatures would give it a second and quite
; different reason to turn one down.
$ORIGIN .
$TTL 3600
@		IN	SOA	ns.root. root.root. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@		IN	NS	ns.root.
ns.root.	IN	A	{{ROOT_ADDR}}
example.	IN	NS	ns.example.
ns.example.	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
elsewhere.	IN	NS	ns.elsewhere.
ns.elsewhere.	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
